1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:04,045
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:15,098
[host] <i>Let's all welcome</i>
<i>the Ardiente family!</i>

3
00:00:15,181 --> 00:00:17,892
[Emilia] <i>You know, Camia Cruz,</i>
<i>if you're telling the truth,</i>

4
00:00:17,976 --> 00:00:20,520
<i>then come out! Show yourself!</i>

5
00:00:20,603 --> 00:00:22,814
[Camia] <i>Are you looking for me?</i>

6
00:00:22,897 --> 00:00:25,316
<i>Well, Emilia. Are you stressed?</i>

7
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:28,820
<i>It's time for you to pay</i>
<i>for what you've done!</i>

8
00:00:28,903 --> 00:00:33,241
<i>I swear no Ardiente will ever hurt</i>
<i>or abuse anyone again!</i>

9
00:00:33,324 --> 00:00:35,618
-[Julio banging cane]
-<i>or abuse anyone again!</i>

10
00:00:35,702 --> 00:00:39,622
[Julio] <i>It's her word against ours.</i>
<i>I'll see you in court.</i>

11
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:42,500
[Emilia] <i>We have to be united</i>
<i>against Camia.</i>

12
00:00:42,584 --> 00:00:45,128
<i>You're right, I agree,</i>
<i>but on one condition.</i>

13
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:48,173
<i>Get rid of Raul! He's a threat.</i>

14
00:00:48,256 --> 00:00:50,717
<i>-I don't trust you anymore.</i>
<i>-I'll change.</i>

15
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,469
<i>I'll earn back your trust in me.</i>

16
00:00:52,552 --> 00:00:54,387
<i>Don't just promise. Do it.</i>

17
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:56,014
[Julio] <i>As for Camia Cruz?</i>

18
00:00:56,097 --> 00:01:00,060
<i>She's nothing without</i>
<i>those witnesses she's hiding.</i>

19
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:02,854
<i>I swear I'll find where they're hiding.</i>

20
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:07,150
[Julio] <i>Make sure that each and</i>
<i>every one of those witnesses</i>

21
00:01:07,233 --> 00:01:11,196
<i>regrets their decision</i>
<i>to go up against the Ardientes.</i>

22
00:01:11,279 --> 00:01:14,574
<i>I want each of them to suffer.</i>

23
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:17,952
<i>-I'm okay, Mom.</i>
<i>-Be careful, Maria.</i>

24
00:01:18,036 --> 00:01:21,164
<i>Text us as soon as you get back</i>
<i>to your aunt's house.</i>

25
00:01:21,247 --> 00:01:23,166
<i>-Let go of me!</i>
-[Raul] <i>Your grandfather already knows</i>

26
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:26,419
<i>where Camia's hiding the witnesses</i>
<i>against the Ardientes.</i>

27
00:01:26,503 --> 00:01:28,797
[Ivy] <i>If you'll keep believing him,</i>

28
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:31,257
<i>maybe I shouldn't trust you either.</i>

29
00:01:31,341 --> 00:01:33,718
<i>It wouldn't hurt to take precautions.</i>

30
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:39,307
[Ivy] Did you notice anything suspicious?

31
00:01:39,390 --> 00:01:40,809
No, ma'am.

32
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:44,020
Tomorrow, more men are coming
to help with security.

33
00:01:44,103 --> 00:01:46,481
All right, ma'am. I'll go back to my post.

34
00:01:46,564 --> 00:01:47,774
Okay.

35
00:01:51,277 --> 00:01:52,570
[line ringing]

36
00:01:54,405 --> 00:01:55,365
Hello, Ivy?

37
00:01:55,448 --> 00:01:56,491
<i>Jepoy…</i>

38
00:01:56,574 --> 00:01:58,868
What's happening in
the Ardiente's mansion?

39
00:01:59,577 --> 00:02:00,870
<i>I spoke to Diego.</i>

40
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:05,250
He said Raul tipped him
off that the Ardientes

41
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:07,168
<i>know where the safe house is.</i>

42
00:02:07,669 --> 00:02:09,504
I don't want to believe Raul

43
00:02:09,587 --> 00:02:11,548
because I don't trust that monster.

44
00:02:12,423 --> 00:02:14,717
But Diego's right too.

45
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:15,969
<i>It wouldn't hurt</i>

46
00:02:16,052 --> 00:02:17,554
to take precautions.

47
00:02:19,681 --> 00:02:21,224
I'll handle it, Ivy. I'll find out.

48
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:26,604
And, Jepoy, if you can, plant
a surveillance camera for us.

49
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:28,606
<i>So we can monitor…</i>

50
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:29,941
the Ardientes' movements.

51
00:02:30,650 --> 00:02:31,651
Okay, copy.

52
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:33,403
Thank you.

53
00:02:43,371 --> 00:02:46,249
[Raul] It doesn't matter to me
if she'll never trust me again.

54
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:50,420
What's important is she's ready
for the Ardientes.

55
00:02:50,503 --> 00:02:52,964
[unsettling music playing]

56
00:02:53,715 --> 00:02:55,800
[Diego] Dad you might
get in trouble for this.

57
00:02:55,925 --> 00:02:58,219
I'd rather get in trouble while fighting

58
00:02:58,303 --> 00:03:01,180
than get in trouble while doing nothing.

59
00:03:02,223 --> 00:03:03,725
But, why are you still there?

60
00:03:04,183 --> 00:03:04,934
<i>Thing is…</i>

61
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:08,479
I can help Camia more if
I stay here with the Ardientes.

62
00:03:09,105 --> 00:03:10,189
<i>Dad, please…</i>

63
00:03:10,273 --> 00:03:12,275
Forget about Mrs. Camia.

64
00:03:12,692 --> 00:03:13,735
<i>I can't do that.</i>

65
00:03:14,193 --> 00:03:15,236
I love Camia.

66
00:03:16,112 --> 00:03:17,697
And I know you don't understand…

67
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:19,657
but I'm begging you.

68
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:21,701
Don't ever leave her.

69
00:03:22,535 --> 00:03:23,745
Always take care of her.

70
00:03:23,953 --> 00:03:25,121
<i>Protect her.</i>

71
00:03:25,204 --> 00:03:27,248
-But, Dad…
-That's all, bye.

72
00:03:29,125 --> 00:03:30,126
Dad!

73
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:33,880
You traitor!

74
00:03:34,505 --> 00:03:35,632
-Who was that?
-Wait!

75
00:03:35,715 --> 00:03:36,466
-Give me that!
-Stop!

76
00:03:36,549 --> 00:03:37,592
Give it to me!

77
00:03:38,509 --> 00:03:39,427
[thuds]

78
00:03:40,595 --> 00:03:42,722
There! You want that? Huh?
Do you still want it?!

79
00:03:42,805 --> 00:03:45,058
I will find out who you're working with!

80
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:48,019
And both of you will suffer!

81
00:03:53,816 --> 00:03:56,277
So, Miss Aguas has
returned to Poblacion Ardiente.

82
00:03:56,361 --> 00:03:57,237
Yes, Mayor.

83
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,947
Did Mama go anywhere else?

84
00:03:59,656 --> 00:04:00,657
No, Mayor.

85
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:02,992
Be sure to accompany her again tomorrow.

86
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:05,245
-Copy that.
-You can go now.

87
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:07,705
Mayor, it looks like you
were celebrating earlier.

88
00:04:07,997 --> 00:04:10,959
Have you found a way
to silence that Camia woman?

89
00:04:11,376 --> 00:04:12,669
I can help you.

90
00:04:13,169 --> 00:04:14,128
What's it to you?

91
00:04:14,212 --> 00:04:16,464
Your assignment
is to look after my mother.

92
00:04:18,383 --> 00:04:20,969
I just wanted to help, Mayor.
I'm sorry for asking.

93
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:25,431
[tense music playing]

94
00:04:55,753 --> 00:04:57,755
[car horn honking]

95
00:05:11,811 --> 00:05:15,231
[Julio] After my TV appearance today…

96
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:19,902
people will definitely forget…

97
00:05:20,361 --> 00:05:21,446
about how…

98
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:25,408
that Camia woman even existed.

99
00:05:25,992 --> 00:05:26,951
And…

100
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:29,454
that'll only happen
if you do things as planned.

101
00:05:29,829 --> 00:05:31,039
I promise you, Grandpa…

102
00:05:31,998 --> 00:05:33,916
the rats will come out of hiding.

103
00:05:34,459 --> 00:05:37,295
-That's what I want to hear.
-Okay, I have to leave now.

104
00:05:37,628 --> 00:05:39,839
-Okay.
-I'll go with you, Mayor.

105
00:05:40,381 --> 00:05:41,674
[Emilia] Oh, wait. Arnaldo…

106
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:44,927
are you leaving?
Is Madrigal going with you?

107
00:05:45,261 --> 00:05:46,429
Why? Do you need him?

108
00:05:46,804 --> 00:05:49,140
Yes. I just have to get rid of something.

109
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:50,600
Get rid of what?

110
00:05:51,225 --> 00:05:52,560
Who could it be?

111
00:05:53,519 --> 00:05:57,690
You know, Emilia,
nothing would make me happier…

112
00:05:58,941 --> 00:06:00,109
if you're talking about Raul.

113
00:06:00,526 --> 00:06:02,528
[Julio laughing]

114
00:06:04,989 --> 00:06:08,159
This day couldn't have been more perfect.

115
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,371
Take care, then.

116
00:06:13,539 --> 00:06:14,540
I'll go now.

117
00:06:19,128 --> 00:06:20,379
Good luck, Emilia.

118
00:06:21,881 --> 00:06:24,509
I better get going too, Papa. Bye.

119
00:06:31,933 --> 00:06:33,518
[Esther] Why did they add more security?

120
00:06:33,935 --> 00:06:35,561
I don't feel good about this, Edward.

121
00:06:35,770 --> 00:06:37,146
Don't think that way, Esther.

122
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:39,565
They just want to protect us.

123
00:06:41,984 --> 00:06:43,986
[Maria whimpering]

124
00:06:48,199 --> 00:06:50,284
[phone vibrating]

125
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:53,412
It's Maria.

126
00:06:55,414 --> 00:06:56,415
Talk to her.

127
00:06:56,707 --> 00:06:57,583
Mom!

128
00:06:59,085 --> 00:07:01,504
Dad! Please help me!

129
00:07:02,338 --> 00:07:03,089
Edward!

130
00:07:03,172 --> 00:07:04,715
-What's wrong?
-Our daughter…

131
00:07:05,967 --> 00:07:08,010
-Please, save me!
-That's enough. Shut her up.

132
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,181
Hello?

133
00:07:12,515 --> 00:07:14,392
<i>If you still want to see</i>
<i>your daughter alive…</i>

134
00:07:14,475 --> 00:07:15,893
you'll come see me.

135
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:18,980
It's Maria.

136
00:07:19,647 --> 00:07:21,482
Why? What happened to her?

137
00:07:21,649 --> 00:07:22,859
[Maria crying]

138
00:07:22,942 --> 00:07:23,943
Here.

139
00:07:27,655 --> 00:07:30,408
[man] We didn't notice anything
suspicious last night, ma'am.

140
00:07:30,616 --> 00:07:31,617
Everything was in order.

141
00:07:31,701 --> 00:07:32,994
Thank you. Mom.

142
00:07:37,081 --> 00:07:38,458
Why? Is there a problem?

143
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:41,335
It's nothing. Don't worry about it.

144
00:07:42,503 --> 00:07:43,504
I want to know.

145
00:07:44,839 --> 00:07:46,841
I spoke to Diego last night.

146
00:07:47,341 --> 00:07:52,054
He said Raul told him
that the Ardientes already know

147
00:07:52,138 --> 00:07:54,474
the location of our witnesses' safe house.

148
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:58,811
-What? How?
-I don't know, Mom.

149
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:01,814
But I asked for additional
security at the safe house.

150
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:13,826
[phone ringing]

151
00:08:16,621 --> 00:08:17,413
Jepoy?

152
00:08:18,289 --> 00:08:19,248
Ivy.

153
00:08:19,332 --> 00:08:20,500
<i>Listen to me.</i>

154
00:08:20,833 --> 00:08:22,502
The Ardientes are making their move.

155
00:08:22,919 --> 00:08:24,337
<i>They're planning something.</i>

156
00:08:24,712 --> 00:08:27,089
I think they're targeting the witnesses.

157
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:28,633
Madrigal!

158
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:32,887
Who was that?

159
00:08:33,554 --> 00:08:34,555
I just checked on the house.

160
00:08:34,931 --> 00:08:35,932
Let's go.

161
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:39,352
[suspenseful music playing]

162
00:08:41,979 --> 00:08:43,773
Mom, I need to go to the safe house.

163
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:46,150
-I'll go with you.
-No need. Just stay here.

164
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:48,778
I'll call you to keep you updated, Mom.

165
00:08:48,861 --> 00:08:50,530
Start the car. We're leaving.

166
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:57,495
The additional security staff
just arrived this morning.

167
00:08:57,995 --> 00:09:00,623
Very good. Do they know
we're on high alert?

168
00:09:00,706 --> 00:09:01,707
Yes, ma'am.

169
00:09:02,833 --> 00:09:04,710
Make sure security is tight.

170
00:09:05,378 --> 00:09:08,172
No one will leave this house
without my knowledge.

171
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:09,840
-Understood?
-Guard.

172
00:09:10,424 --> 00:09:11,926
Have you seen Esther and Edward around?

173
00:09:12,635 --> 00:09:13,594
Why?

174
00:09:13,678 --> 00:09:15,096
We've been looking for them all day.

175
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:17,640
We checked the rooms
but they aren't there.

176
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:19,559
Check the CCTV footage now!

177
00:09:19,642 --> 00:09:21,561
-Yes, ma'am.
-Hurry up!

178
00:09:22,853 --> 00:09:24,021
How did this happen?

179
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:41,330
What do you plan on doing with him?

180
00:09:41,998 --> 00:09:43,666
It depends, Aunt Claire.

181
00:09:43,749 --> 00:09:45,042
Will you have Raul killed?

182
00:09:45,710 --> 00:09:47,461
It depends on his answers.

183
00:09:48,254 --> 00:09:49,630
You two, leave me.

184
00:09:50,881 --> 00:09:52,967
Let me deal with Raul on my own.

185
00:09:58,264 --> 00:09:59,557
[Claire] Let's go, Madrigal.

186
00:10:03,686 --> 00:10:04,645
[door closes]

187
00:10:07,189 --> 00:10:09,984
[ominous music playing]

188
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:16,991
[Emilia giggling]

189
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:18,743
[Emilia sighs]

190
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:27,668
Good morning, my dear husband!
Good morning!

191
00:10:28,085 --> 00:10:28,961
Emilia…

192
00:10:29,712 --> 00:10:31,922
What's the meaning of this?!

193
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:34,717
Why did you? Untie me, Emilia!

194
00:10:35,134 --> 00:10:36,510
Why do you have a gun?

195
00:10:37,178 --> 00:10:37,928
[Raul] Why?

196
00:10:38,012 --> 00:10:38,846
Emilia…

197
00:10:38,929 --> 00:10:40,473
-Well, Raul…
-What's this?!

198
00:10:40,806 --> 00:10:43,517
Bad news. You can't get out of here.

199
00:10:43,601 --> 00:10:45,478
Don't you play with a gun, Emilia.

200
00:10:45,603 --> 00:10:47,396
[humming]

201
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:06,374
Where did you go?

202
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:09,293
Why did you escape?

203
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:15,800
Hurry up!

204
00:11:19,428 --> 00:11:20,304
Maria?

205
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:22,223
-Maria!
-Maria!

206
00:11:22,723 --> 00:11:24,642
-Maria!
-We're home, Maria.

207
00:11:24,725 --> 00:11:25,976
Maria, where are you?

208
00:11:26,394 --> 00:11:27,895
Where's our daughter?!

209
00:11:28,562 --> 00:11:29,563
Where is she?!

210
00:11:29,647 --> 00:11:31,941
Don't move! Stay where you are!
Stay where you are!

211
00:11:32,024 --> 00:11:33,943
-You bastards!
-Where's our daughter?

212
00:11:34,026 --> 00:11:34,944
[Maria] Mom!

213
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:36,237
-Maria!
-Maria!

214
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:37,863
-Maria, my daughter!
-Maria!

215
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:39,115
-Stay here!
-Maria!

216
00:11:39,198 --> 00:11:40,408
-Stay there!
-Maria!

217
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:42,076
You bastards!

218
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:44,245
-What did you do to her?
-Maria!

219
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:46,372
-Mom!
-Maria!

220
00:11:50,334 --> 00:11:52,628
You monsters!

221
00:11:56,674 --> 00:11:59,635
[Raul] Emilia, stop this!
Let me go! Untie me right now!

222
00:11:59,718 --> 00:12:03,305
For what? So you can escape
and see your beloved Camia?

223
00:12:03,681 --> 00:12:05,433
-What's wrong with you?
-Sorry.

224
00:12:05,808 --> 00:12:07,518
Emilia, let's talk about this.

225
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:10,020
No threats or tricks! Put that gun down!

226
00:12:10,104 --> 00:12:11,856
Now, let's play a game.

227
00:12:13,065 --> 00:12:14,358
Truth or dare.

228
00:12:14,442 --> 00:12:16,318
-Emilia.
-I'll ask you a question.

229
00:12:16,402 --> 00:12:17,903
Then, you'll answer it.

230
00:12:17,987 --> 00:12:19,947
If you don't give me the right answer,

231
00:12:20,030 --> 00:12:22,158
I'll close my eyes and shoot you.

232
00:12:22,241 --> 00:12:24,326
-Emilia…
-Who knows where I might…

233
00:12:24,410 --> 00:12:25,661
-Emilia…
-…shoot?

234
00:12:25,744 --> 00:12:27,746
Emilia. Emilia, you don't have to do that.

235
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:29,331
Let's talk about this. Don't do that.

236
00:12:29,415 --> 00:12:32,460
-Question number one.
-Don't point that at me!

237
00:12:32,543 --> 00:12:34,795
Where is Camia Cruz hiding?

238
00:12:36,881 --> 00:12:38,382
I don't know where she is, Emilia!

239
00:12:38,466 --> 00:12:41,469
-Oops, wrong answer.
-Emilia.

240
00:12:41,552 --> 00:12:45,264
[Emilia humming]

241
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:47,183
[Emilia chuckles]

242
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:50,186
-[gunshot]
-[Raul screams]

243
00:12:51,270 --> 00:12:53,272
[laughing maniacally]

244
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:57,401
Oh, I almost got you!

245
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:59,111
Emilia, what are you trying to do?!

246
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:00,029
Don't worry.

247
00:13:00,112 --> 00:13:01,822
Let's play this again tomorrow, okay?

248
00:13:02,781 --> 00:13:04,783
You see, I want you to suffer…

249
00:13:05,701 --> 00:13:07,244
slowly, but surely.

250
00:13:07,328 --> 00:13:09,538
-[laughing maniacally]
-You're crazy, Emilia!

251
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:11,749
Tomorrow again. I'll see you.

252
00:13:11,832 --> 00:13:13,250
-We will play again.
-Emilia, I'm warning you,

253
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:14,877
once I get out of this, you'll regret it.

254
00:13:17,546 --> 00:13:19,131
Bye, my dear husband!

255
00:13:20,925 --> 00:13:22,092
[Raul] You monster!

256
00:13:23,135 --> 00:13:25,429
You're crazy, Emilia! You're insane.

257
00:13:27,306 --> 00:13:28,307
[door closes]

258
00:13:35,856 --> 00:13:38,776
-What is it, Ivy?
-Come with me, Nanny Carlotta.

259
00:13:38,859 --> 00:13:41,946
You should stay at Mom's house.
You're safer there.

260
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:43,531
What's happening, Ivy?

261
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:47,660
Two of our witnesses escaped.

262
00:13:47,993 --> 00:13:51,330
I tried looking for them,
but I couldn't find them.

263
00:13:51,622 --> 00:13:53,707
So I want you to come with me.

264
00:13:55,501 --> 00:13:57,419
I have a bad feeling about this, Nanny.

265
00:13:58,337 --> 00:14:00,548
So you should hide somewhere
else for the time being…

266
00:14:01,215 --> 00:14:02,424
before it's too late.

267
00:14:02,508 --> 00:14:04,260
Okay, I'll just go get my things.

268
00:14:04,885 --> 00:14:06,178
Okay. Hurry, Nanny.

269
00:14:08,806 --> 00:14:09,807
Ivy!

270
00:14:10,975 --> 00:14:11,976
Where are you going?

271
00:14:14,061 --> 00:14:15,020
Let me go with you.

272
00:14:15,646 --> 00:14:16,647
I can help.

273
00:14:25,364 --> 00:14:27,867
-Have mercy on us.
-Please don't hurt my daughter!

274
00:14:27,950 --> 00:14:30,327
I'm begging you! Edward.

275
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:32,746
Where's your safe house, then?

276
00:14:32,997 --> 00:14:33,873
We have no idea.

277
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:36,083
-No! Don't hurt our daughter.
-Really?

278
00:14:36,166 --> 00:14:37,001
[Edward] We don't. Really.

279
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:38,586
-[cocks gun]
-[Esther sobs]

280
00:14:38,711 --> 00:14:39,920
-Edward.
-Camia.

281
00:14:40,004 --> 00:14:43,632
Answer me when I'm asking you!
Where is your safe house?

282
00:14:43,716 --> 00:14:44,925
-Maria!
-Arnaldo! No! Not my daughter!

283
00:14:45,009 --> 00:14:46,594
Okay! Okay! We'll talk!

284
00:14:46,677 --> 00:14:49,972
We'll tell you!
Just don't hurt our daughter!

285
00:14:50,055 --> 00:14:51,974
[Edward] Please! Don't hurt my
daughter! I'm begging you!

286
00:15:02,651 --> 00:15:03,652
[Camia] What?!

287
00:15:04,069 --> 00:15:06,113
Why did they leave the safe house?

288
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,698
I don't know either, Mom.

289
00:15:07,781 --> 00:15:10,284
The CCTV cameras showed
they were talking to someone

290
00:15:10,367 --> 00:15:12,411
on the phone, then they just left.

291
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:15,164
Ivy, you mentioned you

292
00:15:15,247 --> 00:15:17,708
last heard them
talk to their family, right?

293
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:20,169
What if the Ardientes have their daughter?

294
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:22,713
If that's the case,

295
00:15:23,088 --> 00:15:25,090
Esther and Edward are in danger.

296
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:26,508
Not just them,

297
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,761
but all our witnesses.

298
00:15:28,844 --> 00:15:30,846
[tense music playing]

299
00:15:36,894 --> 00:15:37,811
What's going on?

300
00:15:39,396 --> 00:15:40,814
Have the Ardientes found us?!

301
00:15:40,981 --> 00:15:42,149
Tell us!

302
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:46,320
We're dead. I bet Edward
and Esther ratted us out.

303
00:15:46,403 --> 00:15:47,529
I hope not!

304
00:15:47,821 --> 00:15:49,365
[gate creaking]

305
00:15:50,491 --> 00:15:51,575
[gunshots]

306
00:15:53,577 --> 00:15:54,703
[gunshots]

307
00:16:14,974 --> 00:16:15,766
Move! We're leaving!

308
00:16:15,849 --> 00:16:17,226
-What's happening?
-I knew it!

309
00:16:17,309 --> 00:16:18,394
-Let's go!
-Wait for us!

310
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:22,064
Break down the door! Leave no one alive!

311
00:16:25,567 --> 00:16:27,569
[gunshots]

312
00:16:29,738 --> 00:16:31,031
Someone's on the run!

313
00:16:33,409 --> 00:16:34,368
[goon] Stand up!

314
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:39,581
Mayor.

315
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,042
Someone got away.

316
00:16:42,334 --> 00:16:44,336
-Go. Bring them with us.
-Move!

317
00:16:47,256 --> 00:16:48,173
Hurry!

318
00:16:52,678 --> 00:16:54,638
-Did you find him, Madrigal?
-He got away, Mayor.

319
00:16:54,722 --> 00:16:56,306
-He knew where to run.
-It's okay.

320
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:58,267
Thanks to Esther and Edward,

321
00:16:58,642 --> 00:16:59,768
I know where to find him.

322
00:17:02,229 --> 00:17:03,230
Let's go.

323
00:17:06,567 --> 00:17:10,320
The Ardientes probably know
where the safe house is now.

324
00:17:13,198 --> 00:17:14,199
Mom.

325
00:17:14,491 --> 00:17:15,701
I need to transfer them.

326
00:17:16,118 --> 00:17:17,995
I'll move them to another safe house.

327
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:20,039
I need to go there now.

328
00:17:20,372 --> 00:17:21,457
Ivy,

329
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:22,666
I'll go with you.

330
00:17:24,793 --> 00:17:25,878
Okay.

331
00:17:25,961 --> 00:17:26,712
Mom.

332
00:17:26,795 --> 00:17:28,422
-Take care, okay?
-We will.

333
00:17:29,715 --> 00:17:30,966
-Mrs. Camia.
-Take care.

334
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:57,701
Diego.

335
00:18:27,481 --> 00:18:28,690
Diego, check upstairs.

336
00:18:47,417 --> 00:18:48,710
Ivy, they're not there.

337
00:18:51,088 --> 00:18:52,714
They might've escaped.

338
00:18:53,382 --> 00:18:54,675
Diego, let's look for them.

339
00:18:55,467 --> 00:18:56,468
[phone dings]

340
00:18:57,803 --> 00:19:00,722
TONIO IS ALIVE.
PICK HIM UP FROM HIS HOUSE.

341
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:04,101
We need to go somewhere. Come on!

342
00:19:05,894 --> 00:19:07,896
[tense music playing]

343
00:19:16,113 --> 00:19:17,906
Okay, everybody. Let's start.

344
00:19:18,448 --> 00:19:23,245
[crew] Rolling in five,
four, three, two… cue!

345
00:19:24,079 --> 00:19:25,414
[Gino] Congressman Ardiente,

346
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:28,333
thank you for agreeing
to do this interview.

347
00:19:29,042 --> 00:19:31,170
Gino, I should be the one thanking you.

348
00:19:31,253 --> 00:19:33,046
You gave me the opportunity to be heard

349
00:19:33,130 --> 00:19:36,258
by the nation through
your very popular program.

350
00:19:36,341 --> 00:19:38,510
As charismatic as ever, Congressman.

351
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:41,388
And you aren't bothered by the allegations

352
00:19:41,471 --> 00:19:42,848
against you and your family.

353
00:19:43,724 --> 00:19:44,725
But…

354
00:19:45,392 --> 00:19:47,728
let's focus on the issue here.

355
00:19:49,021 --> 00:19:50,147
Camia Cruz.

356
00:19:51,815 --> 00:19:53,400
Is what she's saying true?

357
00:19:54,401 --> 00:19:57,237
Not a word, Gino. Not a word.

358
00:19:58,113 --> 00:20:00,908
And I will take advantage
of the opportunity to say…

359
00:20:01,533 --> 00:20:02,618
truth be told…

360
00:20:03,243 --> 00:20:05,704
I'm the kind of leader who…

361
00:20:06,622 --> 00:20:08,248
works with transparency.

362
00:20:08,332 --> 00:20:09,166
[Arthur] Please, don't!

363
00:20:09,249 --> 00:20:10,334
-Do it.
-Mayor! Mayor!

364
00:20:10,417 --> 00:20:13,378
[Julio] <i>All my actions,</i>
<i>no matter what they are…</i>

365
00:20:14,171 --> 00:20:15,339
<i>are known to the public.</i>

366
00:20:15,881 --> 00:20:17,841
<i>I don't hide anything from them.</i>

367
00:20:18,342 --> 00:20:21,220
That's why in our town,
all our residents know

368
00:20:21,303 --> 00:20:23,013
that I truly care for them.

369
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:26,558
I treat them like my own children.

370
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:28,393
And that's why, in our place,

371
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:31,271
I am fondly known as "Señor Julio".

372
00:20:35,108 --> 00:20:36,693
You're a monster, Arnaldo!

373
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:40,697
You'll burn in hell for this!

374
00:20:42,449 --> 00:20:44,201
You're no different from your family!

375
00:20:44,785 --> 00:20:46,078
You're all evil!

376
00:20:48,038 --> 00:20:52,542
[Julio] <i>These are all</i>
<i>allegations, false allegations.</i>

377
00:20:53,543 --> 00:20:55,170
<i>The worst that</i>
<i>she's throwing at me is that…</i>

378
00:20:56,046 --> 00:20:57,256
[screaming]

379
00:20:58,590 --> 00:21:00,175
…that I'm a murderer?

380
00:21:01,426 --> 00:21:04,680
I'll admit, Gino, it hurts to hear that.

381
00:21:05,347 --> 00:21:06,431
Think about it…

382
00:21:07,849 --> 00:21:10,227
What father can stand…

383
00:21:11,353 --> 00:21:12,396
their children…

384
00:21:13,146 --> 00:21:14,523
getting hurt?

385
00:21:15,148 --> 00:21:18,068
[clamoring]

386
00:21:18,151 --> 00:21:21,446
Shut it. Be quiet. Be quiet!

387
00:21:21,530 --> 00:21:23,699
Shut up and be quiet! [fires shots]

388
00:21:24,074 --> 00:21:25,075
[Julio] <i>Or…</i>

389
00:21:25,784 --> 00:21:27,369
<i>what father can…</i>

390
00:21:28,161 --> 00:21:29,538
-I said shut up!
-<i>stand seeing…</i>

391
00:21:29,621 --> 00:21:32,124
[Julio] <i>any of their loved ones in pain?</i>

392
00:21:34,501 --> 00:21:35,669
To top it off…

393
00:21:37,838 --> 00:21:43,051
what father could ever
kill his own children?

394
00:21:43,427 --> 00:21:44,386
[Arnaldo] Finish them off.

395
00:21:44,469 --> 00:21:46,305
[hostages crying]

396
00:21:46,555 --> 00:21:47,681
[gunshot]

397
00:21:47,806 --> 00:21:49,599
[Maria wailing]

398
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:51,601
[gunshot]

399
00:21:51,810 --> 00:21:53,729
[Maria wailing]

400
00:21:54,771 --> 00:21:55,772
[gunshot]

401
00:21:56,189 --> 00:21:58,567
[Julio] <i>I don't know any father</i>
<i>like that, Gino.</i>

402
00:21:58,650 --> 00:22:00,360
<i>Because the only father I know how to be…</i>

403
00:22:01,236 --> 00:22:04,323
<i>…is a father full of love.</i>

404
00:22:08,827 --> 00:22:10,412
And to my children in Ardiente.

405
00:22:12,497 --> 00:22:13,707
You know the truth.

406
00:22:15,459 --> 00:22:17,961
Your Señor Julio loves you.

407
00:22:20,630 --> 00:22:24,509
[somber music playing]

408
00:22:53,121 --> 00:22:54,956
[tense music playing]

409
00:23:07,928 --> 00:23:09,846
[tense music continues playing]

410
00:23:24,319 --> 00:23:25,153
Let's go.

411
00:23:25,737 --> 00:23:26,655
[Ivy] Hold on.

412
00:23:29,324 --> 00:23:30,325
What's wrong?

413
00:23:30,659 --> 00:23:32,077
We're surrounded.

414
00:23:34,162 --> 00:23:36,123
-What?
-We can't face them all.

415
00:23:36,748 --> 00:23:37,916
Not yet.

416
00:23:43,505 --> 00:23:45,298
We have to secure Tonio.

417
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:52,556
[suspenseful music playing]

418
00:23:59,938 --> 00:24:01,523
Get ready.

419
00:24:04,901 --> 00:24:05,902
[Ivy] Let's go!

420
00:24:06,361 --> 00:24:07,529
[Arnaldo firing shots]

421
00:24:08,196 --> 00:24:09,197
[Ivy] Get in!

422
00:24:10,782 --> 00:24:11,616
Back up!

423
00:24:11,700 --> 00:24:13,535
[gunshots]

424
00:24:19,583 --> 00:24:21,459
-Get down! Get down!
-[Arnaldo] Down! I'll drive!

425
00:24:26,673 --> 00:24:27,674
Hurry, Diego!

426
00:24:29,885 --> 00:24:30,886
They're following us.

427
00:24:34,681 --> 00:24:35,682
[fires shots]

428
00:24:37,142 --> 00:24:38,185
Tonio, get down!

429
00:24:40,854 --> 00:24:42,022
Get down, Tonio!

430
00:24:45,817 --> 00:24:46,818
Madrigal, move!

431
00:24:48,695 --> 00:24:49,696
[grunts]

432
00:24:49,779 --> 00:24:51,281
Hurry, Diego!

433
00:24:56,036 --> 00:24:57,245
Over there!

434
00:25:02,209 --> 00:25:03,335
[tires screeching]

435
00:25:07,464 --> 00:25:08,465
Diego, hurry!

436
00:25:11,593 --> 00:25:12,552
[Ivy grunts]

437
00:25:16,723 --> 00:25:18,141
[tires screeching]

438
00:25:44,209 --> 00:25:45,210
Get up!

439
00:25:48,088 --> 00:25:49,172
[Arnaldo] Stay alert.

440
00:25:53,343 --> 00:25:55,303
[tense music playing]

441
00:26:03,937 --> 00:26:04,813
Over here.

442
00:26:07,565 --> 00:26:08,692
Split up.

443
00:26:11,528 --> 00:26:12,529
Over there, Madrigal.

444
00:27:07,709 --> 00:27:08,710
[quietly] Tonio, let's go.

445
00:27:15,717 --> 00:27:17,719
[tense music playing]

446
00:27:26,728 --> 00:27:27,562
Ivy…

447
00:27:28,146 --> 00:27:29,272
you're hurt.

448
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:31,649
We have to patch it up.

449
00:27:59,844 --> 00:28:00,845
They're here!

450
00:28:04,724 --> 00:28:05,725
[gunshot]

451
00:28:13,983 --> 00:28:14,984
Ivy.

452
00:28:15,151 --> 00:28:16,694
-Jepoy.
-You're hurt.

453
00:28:18,279 --> 00:28:20,323
-I'm fine.
-Get out of here.

454
00:28:21,282 --> 00:28:22,283
Thank you.

455
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:24,661
[Ivy groans]

456
00:28:33,711 --> 00:28:34,712
What happened?

457
00:28:35,547 --> 00:28:36,965
They got Butch, Mayor.

458
00:28:39,259 --> 00:28:40,260
[Arnaldo scoffs]

459
00:28:43,096 --> 00:28:44,472
We had a casualty?!

460
00:28:46,599 --> 00:28:48,226
Seriously?!

461
00:28:49,936 --> 00:28:51,730
What are you doing?! Hmm?

462
00:28:52,147 --> 00:28:54,691
Answer me! Especially you!

463
00:28:55,483 --> 00:28:56,526
Well?!

464
00:28:57,068 --> 00:28:58,695
You good-for-nothing bastards!

465
00:29:01,072 --> 00:29:04,284
Tonio! If you can hear me!

466
00:29:05,744 --> 00:29:06,745
I…

467
00:29:07,495 --> 00:29:09,414
I will kill you myself!

468
00:29:10,123 --> 00:29:11,124
Hear that?!

469
00:29:12,584 --> 00:29:16,421
Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente will kill you!

470
00:29:18,089 --> 00:29:20,759
And to those who are helping you…

471
00:29:21,926 --> 00:29:23,762
I'll kill you all too!

472
00:29:32,687 --> 00:29:33,688
Take him away.

473
00:29:55,668 --> 00:29:57,045
-Daddy!
-Sweetie!

474
00:29:58,046 --> 00:29:59,214
-Ivy!
-Lily!

475
00:30:00,340 --> 00:30:01,382
What happened?!

476
00:30:03,593 --> 00:30:05,678
We had an encounter with Arnaldo's group.

477
00:30:10,058 --> 00:30:12,852
Mom, where are the other witnesses?

478
00:30:14,229 --> 00:30:18,650
Where are Edward, Esther,
and Arthur? Where are they?

479
00:30:19,818 --> 00:30:20,819
Lily…

480
00:30:23,863 --> 00:30:25,448
Your men called me.

481
00:30:27,116 --> 00:30:28,159
What did they say?

482
00:30:31,579 --> 00:30:32,455
Lily…

483
00:30:34,541 --> 00:30:36,417
they're all dead.

484
00:30:38,211 --> 00:30:39,879
[tense music intensifies]

485
00:30:42,590 --> 00:30:43,591
Dead?

486
00:30:53,726 --> 00:30:55,812
All of them?

487
00:30:59,649 --> 00:31:00,692
[Diego pants]

488
00:31:06,155 --> 00:31:07,198
They're all dead?

489
00:31:16,708 --> 00:31:18,001
[screams]

490
00:31:18,710 --> 00:31:20,545
After everything we've done!

491
00:31:21,963 --> 00:31:23,172
Damn it!

492
00:31:24,507 --> 00:31:25,592
They're dead!

493
00:31:25,842 --> 00:31:28,052
-Lily.
-Those monsters!

494
00:31:28,136 --> 00:31:29,971
I'll kill the Ardientes!
I'll kill them all--

495
00:31:30,054 --> 00:31:31,055
[groans]

496
00:31:32,307 --> 00:31:33,808
Lily! Dear!

497
00:31:34,183 --> 00:31:35,184
Ivy!

498
00:31:35,393 --> 00:31:37,103
-Lily.
-Ivy!

499
00:31:38,313 --> 00:31:39,314
Ivy!

500
00:31:39,439 --> 00:31:41,649
-The congressman is coming!
-There he is. There he is.

501
00:31:41,733 --> 00:31:44,694
Ready the mic and camera.

502
00:31:44,777 --> 00:31:45,862
The congressman is here.

503
00:31:46,529 --> 00:31:47,614
Get over here! Come on. Come on.

504
00:31:47,697 --> 00:31:49,032
Start shooting. Start shooting.

505
00:31:49,782 --> 00:31:51,659
-Good morning, Congressman.
-Good day, Congressman.

506
00:31:51,743 --> 00:31:54,621
-Good morning to all of you.
-Congressman Ardiente…

507
00:31:54,704 --> 00:31:56,456
what can you say about
the accusations pointing you

508
00:31:56,539 --> 00:31:58,458
as the one behind the murder
of Camia Cruz's witnesses?

509
00:31:59,208 --> 00:32:00,209
[chuckles]

510
00:32:02,003 --> 00:32:04,255
Why would I do that?

511
00:32:05,048 --> 00:32:09,677
My family and I know
that if something bad happens

512
00:32:09,761 --> 00:32:10,970
to those witnesses,

513
00:32:11,596 --> 00:32:14,682
we'll be the first to blame.

514
00:32:15,016 --> 00:32:16,809
We are innocent.

515
00:32:18,144 --> 00:32:20,146
Don't you realize that yet?

516
00:32:20,813 --> 00:32:25,568
This is propaganda
from our political rivals.

517
00:32:26,527 --> 00:32:27,820
But I have news for them.

518
00:32:29,530 --> 00:32:33,826
The people of Ardiente aren't stupid.

519
00:32:34,786 --> 00:32:37,705
You can't fool them or us.

520
00:32:39,707 --> 00:32:40,708
And…

521
00:32:41,626 --> 00:32:43,252
to all the bereaved families…

522
00:32:44,212 --> 00:32:46,631
we offer our condolences
first and foremost.

523
00:32:47,382 --> 00:32:48,967
But I also assure you…

524
00:32:50,051 --> 00:32:51,970
that the truth will come out,

525
00:32:53,012 --> 00:32:55,807
and justice will be served.

526
00:32:56,349 --> 00:32:58,101
-Now, if you will excuse me.
-I'm sorry.

527
00:32:58,851 --> 00:33:00,353
Just a follow-up question, Congressman.

528
00:33:00,436 --> 00:33:01,771
-What can you say about…
-Excuse us.

529
00:33:01,854 --> 00:33:03,231
…the cases that will be filed against you?

530
00:33:03,314 --> 00:33:04,315
[Julio] I'm sorry.

531
00:33:04,399 --> 00:33:05,525
-How about…
-I have nothing more…

532
00:33:05,608 --> 00:33:07,318
-Camia Cruz, Congressman?
-to say right now.

533
00:33:07,568 --> 00:33:08,861
How are you going to answer back?

534
00:33:08,945 --> 00:33:10,196
One more statement?

535
00:33:13,116 --> 00:33:14,158
[Emilia] My goodness, Papa.

536
00:33:14,242 --> 00:33:16,327
[Julio] Those gossipmongers.

537
00:33:18,204 --> 00:33:21,082
They won't stop talking
and spreading their rumors.

538
00:33:21,165 --> 00:33:23,918
As soon as they hear about an issue…

539
00:33:24,836 --> 00:33:29,549
they'll talk about it
the whole day at the plaza.

540
00:33:31,759 --> 00:33:32,802
[Julio sighs]

541
00:33:32,885 --> 00:33:33,845
Arnaldo,

542
00:33:33,928 --> 00:33:35,555
you look frazzled. I mean…

543
00:33:36,889 --> 00:33:38,725
Is there something you want to tell me?

544
00:33:39,559 --> 00:33:40,727
Tonio escaped, Grandpa.

545
00:33:42,270 --> 00:33:44,605
We don't know who helped him,

546
00:33:44,689 --> 00:33:46,941
but most probably
they're Camia Cruz's men.

547
00:33:47,692 --> 00:33:50,570
We can't trace who owns the car
he used to escape, either.

548
00:33:50,653 --> 00:33:52,697
Papa, we have to find Tonio!

549
00:33:53,031 --> 00:33:56,784
He knows too much about us!
This is not happening.

550
00:33:56,868 --> 00:33:58,036
Arnaldo…

551
00:33:59,579 --> 00:34:02,457
Clean up your mother's mess.

552
00:34:02,999 --> 00:34:08,212
Not for anything else, but
because you are my best soldier.

553
00:34:11,549 --> 00:34:12,717
Don't fail me.

554
00:34:14,343 --> 00:34:18,097
No Ardiente will rot in jail.

555
00:34:20,349 --> 00:34:23,686
Do what you have to do to silence Tonio.

556
00:34:24,187 --> 00:34:26,189
If there are people who would help him…

557
00:34:28,357 --> 00:34:29,358
put a gun to their heads.

558
00:34:31,319 --> 00:34:32,361
Consider it done.

559
00:34:44,874 --> 00:34:46,667
[Julio] Okay, people. May I remind you?

560
00:34:46,751 --> 00:34:50,296
Please, try to avoid
giving statements to the press.

561
00:34:50,755 --> 00:34:52,048
-Hello, everyone.
-Oh.

562
00:34:52,673 --> 00:34:54,926
-Hi, Ivy!
-I'm sorry, I'm late.

563
00:34:55,176 --> 00:34:56,385
-Hi, Mayor.
-That's okay.

564
00:34:56,469 --> 00:34:57,637
I'm glad you came.

565
00:34:57,845 --> 00:35:00,723
-Good evening, Miss Aguas.
-Congressman. Emilia. Hello.

566
00:35:00,807 --> 00:35:02,350
You missed all the action.

567
00:35:03,643 --> 00:35:04,727
What are you referring to?

568
00:35:04,811 --> 00:35:10,316
The accusations that your family
had all those witnesses killed?

569
00:35:10,983 --> 00:35:13,778
Emilia, I know all the details. Thank you.

570
00:35:14,529 --> 00:35:16,864
Like, um… What did the media say about us?

571
00:35:17,698 --> 00:35:20,618
The usual. That you're all corrupt.

572
00:35:21,119 --> 00:35:22,120
Heartless.

573
00:35:22,912 --> 00:35:23,913
Criminals.

574
00:35:24,330 --> 00:35:25,331
In short…

575
00:35:26,707 --> 00:35:27,708
dirty.

576
00:35:33,714 --> 00:35:35,883
Sorry for asking this, but…

577
00:35:36,717 --> 00:35:37,927
Are you guilty?

578
00:35:39,512 --> 00:35:40,680
Of course not.

579
00:35:40,972 --> 00:35:44,142
[Arnaldo] We play fair.
We didn't have anyone killed.

580
00:35:44,684 --> 00:35:47,019
[Ivy] You have a point, Mr. Mayor.

581
00:35:47,436 --> 00:35:48,437
Only…

582
00:35:48,771 --> 00:35:53,359
a merciless person could do such a thing.

583
00:35:53,442 --> 00:35:55,194
And if you ask me,

584
00:35:55,820 --> 00:35:57,780
they deserve to rot in prison,

585
00:35:57,864 --> 00:36:00,116
or, perhaps, die too.

586
00:36:01,576 --> 00:36:02,869
Right, Congressman?

587
00:36:03,452 --> 00:36:05,037
You couldn't be more right.

588
00:36:07,707 --> 00:36:11,210
Did you know that one
of the witnesses survived?

589
00:36:11,294 --> 00:36:15,089
Yes, Antonio Vidal, my former bodyguard.

590
00:36:16,215 --> 00:36:18,384
So, do you know where he's hiding?

591
00:36:18,467 --> 00:36:20,136
Honestly, Miss Aguas…

592
00:36:20,219 --> 00:36:23,514
we won't waste our time
pondering that issue.

593
00:36:24,265 --> 00:36:26,726
Besides, we're ready for whatever

594
00:36:26,809 --> 00:36:29,103
they're going to throw at us in court.

595
00:36:29,770 --> 00:36:30,771
[Arnaldo] That's right.

596
00:36:31,063 --> 00:36:32,815
I hope you'll be there
during the arraignment.

597
00:36:33,316 --> 00:36:34,650
We need your support.

598
00:36:36,110 --> 00:36:40,031
Of course, Mr. Mayor.
As always, you can count on me.

599
00:36:40,615 --> 00:36:41,908
That's what I like about you.

600
00:36:42,491 --> 00:36:44,076
You never fail us.

601
00:36:44,577 --> 00:36:47,705
So I hope our relationship
continues to improve.

602
00:36:51,250 --> 00:36:52,585
Mr. Mayor…

603
00:36:56,047 --> 00:36:57,840
not so fast.

604
00:36:58,883 --> 00:37:01,093
I haven't even finished
the main course yet.

605
00:37:01,719 --> 00:37:03,137
Let's save that for dessert.

606
00:37:04,931 --> 00:37:06,224
[Ivy] Excuse me.

607
00:37:06,307 --> 00:37:07,725
I need to go to the ladies' room.

608
00:37:16,901 --> 00:37:17,735
Mayor…

609
00:37:18,945 --> 00:37:20,738
Okay. Excuse me.

610
00:37:21,489 --> 00:37:22,531
Go ahead.

611
00:37:25,701 --> 00:37:26,994
-Yes?
-Mayor.

612
00:37:27,662 --> 00:37:29,622
Everything you want to know about Tonio

613
00:37:29,705 --> 00:37:31,582
and his family is in here.

614
00:37:31,666 --> 00:37:33,626
[tense music playing]

615
00:37:36,837 --> 00:37:37,838
Thank you.

616
00:37:37,922 --> 00:37:39,090
-We'll go now, Mayor.
-Okay.

617
00:37:46,639 --> 00:37:48,015
I'll be in my office.

618
00:37:48,641 --> 00:37:51,519
Make sure no one bothers me. Understood?

619
00:37:52,019 --> 00:37:53,020
Yes, Mayor.

620
00:37:56,232 --> 00:37:58,234
[tense music playing]

621
00:38:04,782 --> 00:38:05,783
[chimes]

622
00:38:41,110 --> 00:38:43,988
[tense music playing]

623
00:38:58,294 --> 00:38:59,795
[knocks]

624
00:38:59,879 --> 00:39:00,796
Ivy?

625
00:39:02,506 --> 00:39:04,383
Ivy, open up…

626
00:39:05,885 --> 00:39:07,636
Ivy, are you there?

627
00:39:09,180 --> 00:39:10,681
Ivy, can we talk?

628
00:39:11,557 --> 00:39:13,392
Um… Just a minute!

629
00:39:13,559 --> 00:39:14,602
[Emilia] Okay.

630
00:39:15,519 --> 00:39:19,231
[suspenseful music playing]

631
00:39:26,447 --> 00:39:27,448
Yes?

632
00:39:27,573 --> 00:39:28,657
Ivy, can we talk?

633
00:39:29,867 --> 00:39:30,868
Sure!

634
00:39:32,119 --> 00:39:33,120
About what?

635
00:39:40,211 --> 00:39:42,755
-Fernandez.
-Madrigal. What is it?

636
00:39:43,714 --> 00:39:45,174
I have something to report to Mayor.

637
00:39:45,466 --> 00:39:47,593
I'm sorry.
He doesn't want to be disturbed.

638
00:39:48,803 --> 00:39:50,971
-He said that?
-Before he went in.

639
00:39:55,601 --> 00:39:56,602
All right.

640
00:40:08,197 --> 00:40:10,032
[Emilia] It's actually about Raul.

641
00:40:10,825 --> 00:40:11,992
Oh. What about him?

642
00:40:12,701 --> 00:40:14,203
It's just between us, okay?

643
00:40:15,037 --> 00:40:16,247
You know, I think…

644
00:40:17,540 --> 00:40:19,708
he's in love with Camia Cruz.

645
00:40:19,792 --> 00:40:21,168
He's obsessed with her.

646
00:40:21,710 --> 00:40:22,920
[tense music playing]

647
00:40:23,003 --> 00:40:24,547
The Camia Cruz?

648
00:40:25,172 --> 00:40:26,715
Yes, the one and only!

649
00:40:27,883 --> 00:40:29,927
To be fair though, Emilia,

650
00:40:30,594 --> 00:40:32,847
Camia Cruz seems nice.

651
00:40:33,514 --> 00:40:36,183
And I find her really beautiful.

652
00:40:36,267 --> 00:40:40,438
It's no wonder Raul is
head over heels in love with her.

653
00:40:40,521 --> 00:40:41,689
Shut up!

654
00:40:42,398 --> 00:40:43,399
It's true!

655
00:40:43,941 --> 00:40:44,942
I'm just being frank.

656
00:40:45,693 --> 00:40:50,114
I don't choose my words
just to gently reassure you.

657
00:40:50,197 --> 00:40:51,615
I'm not like that.

658
00:40:51,699 --> 00:40:53,534
So, what will I do now?

659
00:40:54,660 --> 00:40:56,245
Well, if I were you,

660
00:40:56,328 --> 00:40:58,164
I'd put a leash around his neck

661
00:40:58,247 --> 00:41:03,335
so he couldn't escape
and go sniffing around other women.

662
00:41:03,544 --> 00:41:06,797
-I already did!
-Make it tighter, then.

663
00:41:06,881 --> 00:41:10,968
Ivy, if I do that, what if he
tries to break away even more?

664
00:41:11,343 --> 00:41:13,762
Let him go, then. Just like that.

665
00:41:14,847 --> 00:41:16,724
Let your husband go.

666
00:41:17,183 --> 00:41:22,688
I mean, sure, you can give
that man another chance.

667
00:41:23,022 --> 00:41:26,275
Then another second chance,
a third, a fourth.

668
00:41:26,817 --> 00:41:30,571
Let's see how much you can bear
being a martyr in love.

669
00:41:31,572 --> 00:41:35,493
I guess you're right, Ivy.
You know, I am all that I am.

670
00:41:35,826 --> 00:41:39,830
But I guess, when it comes
to love, it is my weakness.

671
00:41:40,206 --> 00:41:41,999
Love really is stupid.

672
00:41:42,750 --> 00:41:45,002
But, yeah, I'll try that.

673
00:41:45,127 --> 00:41:48,130
Emilia, Raul is the least
of your problems.

674
00:41:48,631 --> 00:41:50,174
You've got bigger fish to fry.

675
00:41:50,591 --> 00:41:53,177
You're facing numerous legal cases.

676
00:41:54,553 --> 00:41:55,679
Like Tonio.

677
00:41:56,222 --> 00:41:59,975
What if he testifies? What will happen?

678
00:42:00,100 --> 00:42:04,021
Can't you do something to keep him quiet?

679
00:42:05,481 --> 00:42:06,649
You know, Ivy?

680
00:42:06,732 --> 00:42:08,692
Honestly, I have no answer for that.

681
00:42:10,110 --> 00:42:11,111
[sighs]

682
00:42:12,530 --> 00:42:15,866
Well, as your friend,
if you get sent to jail,

683
00:42:16,033 --> 00:42:17,826
I'll visit you every day.

684
00:42:18,202 --> 00:42:19,036
Yeah, right!

685
00:42:19,119 --> 00:42:20,287
[giggles]

686
00:42:21,205 --> 00:42:23,916
Emilia, I just wanted
to lighten things up.

687
00:42:23,999 --> 00:42:25,084
Don't be silly.

688
00:42:25,709 --> 00:42:28,546
Trust me. I support you.

689
00:42:28,921 --> 00:42:30,965
And I appreciate that. Let's go.

690
00:42:32,550 --> 00:42:33,425
[chuckles]

691
00:42:46,647 --> 00:42:48,315
[tense music playing]

692
00:42:55,030 --> 00:42:56,615
Love me, Raul.

693
00:42:57,575 --> 00:42:58,701
Please.

694
00:42:59,368 --> 00:43:00,578
Love me back.

695
00:43:01,829 --> 00:43:03,247
That's all I ask of you.

696
00:43:04,582 --> 00:43:06,500
Then take back your threats against Diego.

697
00:43:08,961 --> 00:43:10,337
Show me you love me first.

698
00:43:24,935 --> 00:43:25,936
Mom.

699
00:43:28,397 --> 00:43:29,398
Ivy…

700
00:43:30,691 --> 00:43:32,484
Are you ready for the arraignment?

701
00:43:33,152 --> 00:43:34,403
Honestly, I'm nervous.

702
00:43:35,321 --> 00:43:36,947
What if we lose?

703
00:43:37,698 --> 00:43:38,699
Mom, no.

704
00:43:39,116 --> 00:43:40,784
We can't lose.

705
00:43:41,452 --> 00:43:43,162
We have a high chance of winning this case

706
00:43:43,245 --> 00:43:45,581
because of Tonio's statement against them.

707
00:43:47,541 --> 00:43:50,252
Besides, Dad is watching over us.

708
00:43:51,879 --> 00:43:54,048
I know he will help us.

709
00:44:12,232 --> 00:44:14,234
I'm still willing to make
this marriage work.

710
00:44:15,778 --> 00:44:17,029
You're still my husband.

711
00:44:17,946 --> 00:44:19,156
You're mine.

712
00:44:21,283 --> 00:44:22,284
Get dressed.

713
00:44:22,368 --> 00:44:24,036
Our arraignment is scheduled at 9 AM.

714
00:44:30,167 --> 00:44:32,294
[dramatic music]

715
00:44:33,712 --> 00:44:35,464
-Miss Aguas.
-Mr. Mayor.

716
00:44:35,547 --> 00:44:36,548
I'm glad you made it.

717
00:44:36,632 --> 00:44:39,843
Of course, this is the most
controversial case of the year.

718
00:44:39,927 --> 00:44:41,679
So, I can't miss it.

719
00:44:42,012 --> 00:44:44,640
-How are you, Miss Aguas?
-I'm okay.

720
00:44:45,099 --> 00:44:46,266
Excuse us.

721
00:44:55,234 --> 00:44:56,068
[Raul] Camia.

722
00:44:56,151 --> 00:44:59,405
One stupid move, Raul.
And you'll mourn for Diego.

723
00:44:59,530 --> 00:45:01,198
[tense music playing]

724
00:45:03,575 --> 00:45:05,160
Good morning, Miss Cruz.

725
00:45:07,121 --> 00:45:09,581
Diego. Attorney.

726
00:45:12,751 --> 00:45:16,713
I hope we can clear things out soon.

727
00:45:17,339 --> 00:45:18,424
You know, Miss Cruz…

728
00:45:19,341 --> 00:45:20,801
we aren't your enemies.

729
00:45:23,595 --> 00:45:25,973
Drop the act, Congressman.

730
00:45:27,558 --> 00:45:29,476
No one believes you now.

731
00:45:41,071 --> 00:45:43,699
[court clerk] All rise.
The court is now in session.

732
00:45:44,241 --> 00:45:47,411
The honorable judge
Vincent Legazpi presiding.

733
00:45:48,287 --> 00:45:49,371
[judge bangs gavel]

734
00:45:50,038 --> 00:45:51,957
People of the Philippines versus Emilia

735
00:45:52,040 --> 00:45:54,543
Ardiente-Torillo and Raul Torillo.

736
00:45:54,626 --> 00:46:00,424
Criminal case number 3246950
for conspiracy to commit rape,

737
00:46:00,507 --> 00:46:04,636
case number 3246783 for attempted murder,

738
00:46:04,720 --> 00:46:08,015
and case number 3256109
for illegal detention.

739
00:46:09,975 --> 00:46:10,851
Let's proceed.

740
00:46:11,727 --> 00:46:13,729
[tense music playing]

741
00:46:28,410 --> 00:46:29,620
The prosecution calls

742
00:46:29,703 --> 00:46:31,788
Mr. Antonio Vidal to the witness stand.

743
00:46:58,148 --> 00:46:59,691
Please raise your right hand.

744
00:47:01,485 --> 00:47:03,820
Do you solemnly swear to tell the truth,

745
00:47:03,904 --> 00:47:05,614
and nothing but the truth?

746
00:47:06,823 --> 00:47:07,824
I do.

747
00:47:12,037 --> 00:47:13,038
Mr. Vidal…

748
00:47:13,705 --> 00:47:15,624
can you please tell the court

749
00:47:15,707 --> 00:47:18,835
what your connection
to the Ardiente family was?

750
00:47:20,587 --> 00:47:23,757
I used to be a bodyguard for
former governor Emilia Torillo.

751
00:47:24,925 --> 00:47:27,511
So, as Mrs. Torillo's former bodyguard,

752
00:47:27,844 --> 00:47:29,471
what were your duties?

753
00:47:32,140 --> 00:47:34,643
My duty was to ensure
her safety and security…

754
00:47:35,102 --> 00:47:36,603
and to protect her and her family

755
00:47:36,687 --> 00:47:38,689
from anyone who threatened them.

756
00:47:39,064 --> 00:47:40,607
Was it also your duty

757
00:47:40,691 --> 00:47:43,610
to obey whatever
Mrs. Torillo ordered you to do?

758
00:47:44,319 --> 00:47:45,279
Yes, your Honor.

759
00:47:46,488 --> 00:47:48,282
Did you do everything she told you to?

760
00:47:49,241 --> 00:47:50,826
She was my boss, your Honor.

761
00:47:51,743 --> 00:47:54,788
Of course, I would carry out her orders.

762
00:47:56,665 --> 00:47:59,876
Even if it was to kill innocent people?

763
00:48:06,425 --> 00:48:07,634
If she told me to,

764
00:48:08,385 --> 00:48:09,344
I'd do it.

765
00:48:11,638 --> 00:48:16,351
Mr. Vidal, did former governor
Emilia Torillo

766
00:48:16,435 --> 00:48:20,230
order you to rape and kill Camia Cruz,

767
00:48:20,314 --> 00:48:24,484
wife of Atty. Dante Cruz,
a critic of the Ardientes?

768
00:48:24,568 --> 00:48:27,321
[tense music playing]

769
00:48:36,455 --> 00:48:37,497
I repeat.

770
00:48:39,499 --> 00:48:44,546
Did the former governor order you
to rape and kill Camia Cruz?

771
00:48:52,554 --> 00:48:53,889
No, your Honor.

772
00:48:53,972 --> 00:48:56,975
[tense music playing]

773
00:49:12,991 --> 00:49:15,243
[Emilia] <i>Camia. Camia, darling.</i>

774
00:49:15,327 --> 00:49:16,787
<i>Even if you have me killed now,</i>

775
00:49:16,870 --> 00:49:19,289
<i>your husband will never love you!</i>

776
00:49:19,373 --> 00:49:20,749
<i>So you really want more?!</i>

777
00:49:21,208 --> 00:49:22,709
[Ivy] <i>Emilia, that's enough!</i>

778
00:49:23,126 --> 00:49:26,546
[Emilia] <i>You're right about Ivy.</i>
<i>She's just playing with us.</i>

779
00:49:26,630 --> 00:49:28,590
<i>I don't know if she's</i>
<i>only just convinced Diego</i>

780
00:49:28,674 --> 00:49:30,884
<i>or if they've always been accomplices.</i>

781
00:49:30,967 --> 00:49:34,971
[Julio] <i>We can't trust anyone anymore.</i>

782
00:49:35,055 --> 00:49:38,475
<i>I want you to keep an eye on Madrigal.</i>

783
00:49:38,558 --> 00:49:39,768
<i>You have to see this.</i>

784
00:49:40,227 --> 00:49:41,937
<i>Good work, Arnaldo.</i>

785
00:49:42,020 --> 00:49:44,815
<i>We finally caught the rat.</i>

786
00:49:44,898 --> 00:49:48,402
[theme music playing]
